{
  "version": 1,
  "name": "Two-storey house, ground floor and upper floor with internal stair",
  "units": "m",
  "meta": {
    "source": "image",
    "scale_note": "I used the printed 9.35 m dimension line. It spans about 748 px, which gives 80 px/m. I took it as the centerline length of the outer walls. The printed room areas match the resulting polygons closely (for example Living 25.0, Dining 14.3, Landing 15.1), so I am fairly sure of the scale.",
    "notes": "Origin is the top-left outer corner of each floor, and both floors use the same footprint. Wall thickness is about 0.3 m. Window and door positions are read from pixels and are approximate. I left out the small windows on the right wall of the ground floor and some on the upper floor, because they were unclear. Stair step counts are estimated at about 16. The kitchen counters, WC fixtures, bathtub, round columns and the kitchen island are not included. The ground floor kitchen/living and living/dining boundaries are drawn as open edges, with partial partitions only. The upper-floor stair is the same flight as the ground floor stair, drawn in the opposite direction. Furniture is limited to the clearest pieces."
  },
